consumer(path=>path.includes('.restartPolicy')&&!path.includes('.resizePolicy'),'With ContainerRestartRules enabled, the runtime examines rules in stored order and uses the first In/NotIn rule matching the exit code. Restart requests restart; RestartAllContainers requires its runtime feature or falls back to policy. Without a matching action it uses container Always/Never/OnFailure, then Pod policy. Deleted Pods and already running containers do not restart; absent historical status starts a container.',[source('pkg/api/v1/pod/util.go','419-492','Original restart evaluation chooses the first matching rule and then container/Pod policies.'),source('pkg/kubelet/container/helpers.go','82-119','The runtime restart entry point handles deletion, missing/running status and the ContainerRestartRules gate.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','1788-1812','Disabled restart-rule preparation clears regular overrides/rules, non-Always init policies and all init rules.')],['exact ordered rule runtime evaluation']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${p}.resources`)||path.startsWith(`${p}.resourceClaims`)||path.includes('.resources.claims'),'Deployment preparation drops Pod resources when PodLevelResources is disabled and absent from the old spec. It drops Pod resourceClaims and container claim references when DynamicResourceAllocation is disabled and not in use by the old spec; retained values still undergo their selected validators.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','900-907','Pod-level resource drop depends on the gate and old-object use.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','1092-1100','DRA drop clears Pod claims and container claim references.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','417-485','Validation options read feature gates and preserve old object compatibility.')],['Disabled-field dropping','feature-enabled validation option']);
