consumer(path=>path.includes('.resourceFieldRef'),'A zero divisor becomes quantity 1 in the extractor. CPU scales MilliValue and other supported resources scale Value; results round upward with math.Ceil. A nonempty container name searches regular then init containers and fails if absent. Downward volume extraction deep-copies the found container and fills absent or zero CPU/memory/ephemeral-storage limits from node allocatable before scaling; environment extraction without an explicit name reads the current container.',[source('pkg/api/v1/resource/helpers.go','80-205','The original resource extractor implements container lookup, zero divisor fallback, ceiling scaling and node-allocatable limit fallback.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kubelet_pods.go','1026-1037','Environment resource selection uses current-container extraction for an empty name.')],['exact runtime scaling fallback','Exact scaling for zero']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.automountServiceAccountToken`||path===`${p}.serviceAccountName`||path.startsWith(`${p}.imagePullSecrets`),'On created Pod admission, an empty serviceAccountName becomes default; lookup errors forbid admission. Pod automount preference wins over ServiceAccount preference, then defaults true. With token mounting enabled and this effective preference true, admission adds token mounts unless the mount path is already used. If imagePullSecrets is empty, admission copies ServiceAccount imagePullSecrets; a nonempty authored list is retained.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/serviceaccount/admission.go','148-176','ServiceAccount admission defaults and resolves the account, mounts permitted tokens and fills only an empty imagePullSecrets list.'),source('plugin/pkg/admission/serviceaccount/admission.go','254-265','Automount precedence is Pod, ServiceAccount, then true.')],['ServiceAccount admission plugin','Image pull credential selection']);
consumer(path=>['priority','priorityClassName','preemptionPolicy'].some(x=>path===`${p}.${x}`),'Created Pod Priority admission resolves the named class or the global default. A missing named class rejects admission. A supplied numerical priority differing from the computed class value rejects admission; otherwise admission writes the computed value. When the class supplies preemptionPolicy, a different authored policy rejects admission and the class policy is written. Pod update fills only omitted values from stored values; immutable Pod validation still applies.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/priority/admission.go','137-204','Priority admission distinguishes create class resolution/conflicts from update preservation.'),source('plugin/pkg/admission/priority/admission.go','228-256','Default priority chooses a global default class or zero.')],['Priority admission']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.runtimeClassName`||path.startsWith(`${p}.overhead`)||path.startsWith(`${p}.nodeSelector`),'Created Pod RuntimeClass admission performs cache then API lookup; a missing named class rejects admission. Class overhead replaces absent/empty authored overhead but a different nonempty map rejects admission; validation rejects nonnil Pod overhead with no corresponding class overhead. Class node selectors merge with authored keys, reject differing values for the same key, and add nonconflicting keys; class tolerations merge with Pod tolerations.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/runtimeclass/admission.go','142-238','RuntimeClass admission implements lookup, exact overhead conflicts and node selector/toleration merge.')],['RuntimeClass admission lookup','RuntimeClass admission can supply overhead']);
consumer(path=>/\.affinity\.pod(?:Anti)?Affinity/.test(path),'Affinity terms match Pod labels AND the union of explicitly listed namespaces and namespace-selector matches. When the namespace list is empty and namespaceSelector is nil, the scheduler inserts the incoming Pod namespace. A nonnil empty namespace selector selects every namespace; nil selects none through the general converter. Required incoming terms resolve a nonempty namespace selector into the namespace-name set before filtering.',[source('staging/src/k8s.io/kube-scheduler/framework/types.go','377-391','AffinityTerm matches namespace membership or namespace-selector labels together with Pod selector.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/kube-scheduler/framework/types.go','419-445','Affinity term conversion and own-namespace fallback depend on nil selector and empty namespace list.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/interpodaffinity/plugin.go','137-157','Incoming term namespace-selector results merge into the explicit namespace set.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/interpodaffinity/filtering.go','274-309','Required incoming affinity and anti-affinity namespace sets are prepared before filtering.')],['Exact scheduler fallback','scheduler-specific namespace fallback']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.affinity.nodeAffinity')&&!path.includes('.preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution'),'Required node affinity ORs terms and ANDs each term label and field requirements. Empty terms select no nodes. Gt/Lt requires exactly one base-10 signed int64 value at selector construction; missing or nonnumeric node label values do not match. Gt is strictly greater and Lt strictly less. A parse error is returned only if no alternative term matches.',[source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/scheduling/corev1/nodeaffinity/nodeaffinity.go','61-105','Empty terms are skipped and alternatives use lazy OR matching.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/scheduling/corev1/nodeaffinity/nodeaffinity.go','202-253','Node requirements convert to the concrete label selector operators.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','185-215','Gt/Lt construction parses one decimal int64 operand.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','265-292','Gt/Lt matching requires a present parseable node label and strict integer comparison.')],['Empty node-selector terms require','Gt/Lt parsing']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${p}.topologySpreadConstraints`),'The scheduler converts the label selector and ANDs equality requirements for matchLabelKeys present in the incoming Pod labels; absent Pod-label keys add no requirement. Nil minDomains uses 1, nil nodeAffinityPolicy uses Honor and nil nodeTaintsPolicy uses Ignore. Enabled inclusion policies apply their retained overrides. Honor filters node affinity or untolerated scheduling taints; Ignore omits that respective filter.',[source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/podtopologyspread/common.go','42-55','Honor inclusion policies filter node affinity and taints.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/podtopologyspread/common.go','86-142','Concrete spread selector, matched label keys and nil policy/min-domain defaults are constructed here.')],['Scheduler selector construction is a separate','Every topology-spread child']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.affinity')||path.startsWith(`${p}.topologySpreadConstraints`),'API preparation drops match/mismatch keys if the associated feature is disabled and not already in use by the old spec. Retained selectors and keys receive the selected strict or old-object compatibility options; a disabled gate is not permission to infer that a supplied retained field reached the scheduler.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','1164-1205','Feature-dependent field dropping distinguishes Pod affinity and topology spread.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','417-485','Validation options combine gates with old-selector compatibility.')],['Each key item and exact merge','Complete recursive node-selector']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.emptyDir`),'The emptyDir plugin accepts the default medium, Memory or a hugepage medium; other media fail setup with unknown storage medium. Memory size is the minimum positive applicable bound of node allocatable memory, Pod memory limit and authored sizeLimit; zero sizeLimit does not lower it. Setup mounts tmpfs/hugetlbfs or creates a directory and applies group ownership. Disk quota assignment depends on filesystem support; this path is not a universal hard disk-capacity limit.',[source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','114-165','Memory emptyDir size selection excludes zero and uses node/Pod/volume bounds.'),source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','234-317','Setup chooses supported media, ownership and optional filesystem quota assignment.'),source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','318-388','Memory and hugepage volume mount construction uses the chosen size and page size.')],['Storage medium support','Node medium support','API acceptance does not establish']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(trust),'The informer trust manager requires synchronized cache. On cache misses, named NotFound or zero signer/selector matches returns empty data only with optional true; other lookup/conversion errors fail. Signer selection converts nil to match nothing and {} to match everything and filters by exact signerName on the lookup route. Before lookup/optional handling it checks a key of signerName and selector.String(); nil and {} both stringify to the empty string, so a prior successful {} result can be returned to a later nil lookup. Successful entries are normalized/deduplicated and expire with cacheTTL; informer invalidation removes matching signer keys for signed bundles or matching name keys for unsigned bundles. A named signed-bundle key can survive signer invalidation. Serialized selectors over 100 KiB fail. A no-op manager rejects the operation. This shared-key limitation is a static deduction, not a live lookup.',[source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','169-194','Informer events invalidate normalized trust cache entries.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','197-280','Actual trust lookup selects name or signer/labels and implements missing-result handling.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','326-335','A no-op trust manager rejects trust lookups.')],['Feature enablement, bundle existence','General nil-selector conversion']);
