consumer(path=>unsupportedSources.some(branch=>path===`${v}.${branch}`||path.startsWith(`${v}.${branch}.`)),'This retained historical source can pass API validation, but the pinned standard kubelet does not register an implementation for this branch and it is not one of the listed CSI migrations. Volume plugin selection therefore fails instead of mounting it. Blocked step: mount this source with the standard binary. Safe action: have the storage operator select a supported CSI/PVC source and rewrite the manifest. Owner: cluster storage operator. Follow-up: verify the replacement driver is registered and the replacement Pod volume reaches successful mount before application startup.',[source('cmd/kubelet/app/plugins.go','28-83','The standard binary enumerates its volume plugins, including CSI and supported in-tree branches.'),source('cmd/kubelet/app/plugins_providers.go','59-70','The remaining provider registration is Portworx, controlled by its unregister feature.'),source('pkg/volume/csimigration/plugin_manager.go','56-108','Only enumerated legacy providers have a CSI migration route.'),source('pkg/volume/plugins.go','631-665','Plugin selection returns ErrNoPluginMatched if no registered plugin supports the spec.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.csi`),'For inline CSI, the node requires Ephemeral lifecycle support in CSIDriver. The mounter passes fsType, volumeAttributes and readOnly to NodePublishVolume. A nodePublishSecretRef is resolved in the Pod namespace; every Secret data byte value is converted to a string map for the driver, without an API-level fixed credential-key schema. Lookup failure is a transient mount failure. Driver RPC failure fails setup; API acceptance alone does not establish a driver/backend mount.',[source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','120-176','Inline CSI uses Ephemeral lifecycle and namespace-local NodePublishSecretRef.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','217-251','Node-publish credentials and selected Pod token attributes are prepared.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','300-335','The actual NodePublishVolume call passes the effective readOnly/fsType/attributes/secret fields and handles errors.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_util.go','45-56','Secret credentials copy every data entry as a string.')],['CSIDriver lifecycle modes','external or migrated storage driver','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.secret`)||path.startsWith(`${v}.configMap`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.secret`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.configMap`),'The kubelet object managers choose API reads, TTL cache or informer watch propagation. Plugins reassemble file payloads on remount and use an atomic writer, so manager propagation and the next remount determine update visibility. A subPath mount binds the selected path separately; rewriting the parent volume payload does not replace the existing bind mount. Optional applies only to the stated missing-object/key paths, not arbitrary API errors.',[source('pkg/kubelet/secret/secret_manager.go','116-161','Caching and watching Secret managers define retrieval/propagation routes.'),source('pkg/kubelet/configmap/configmap_manager.go','114-160','Caching and watching ConfigMap managers define retrieval/propagation routes.'),source('pkg/volume/util/atomic_writer.go','86-120','Atomic writer publishes new payload data through timestamp directories and symlink replacement.')],['Existence, key selection, optional handling','Refresh, subPath update visibility']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.downwardAPI`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.downwardAPI`),'Downward payload construction reads the created Pod fields, cleans each output path, selects the per-item mode over fallback mode and aggregates extraction errors. Duplicate paths in a direct downwardAPI payload use the later map write; projected explicit duplicates are rejected by API validation. Updating Pod fields is observed only when the plugin collects and republishes a new payload.',[source('pkg/volume/downwardapi/downwardapi.go','238-277','CollectData performs exact path/mode selection, field/resource extraction and map writes.')],['runtime extractor and file update']);
