for(const field of ['lastUpdateTime','lastTransitionTime']) statusRecord(`$.status.conditions[].${field}`,`Report condition ${field}.`,'An omitted Time value stays zero.','An explicit empty string fails RFC3339 time parsing.','Nonstring values or strings that do not parse as RFC3339 fail Time.UnmarshalJSON; this numeric status validator adds no relative timestamp check.',{nullValue:'Time.UnmarshalJSON(null) resets the Time value to zero; it is not an ordinary string null dispatch.',evidence:[...conditionEvidence,source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/apis/meta/v1/time.go','99-120','Time JSON decoding explicitly zeros null and parses every other value as RFC3339.')]});
const migrations=[
 ['awsElasticBlockStore','aws_ebs.go','104-137','AWS translation normalizes volumeID into the CSI handle, passes fsType/readOnly and formats partition as a decimal volume attribute. Invalid provider ID translation fails before node publishing.'],
 ['gcePersistentDisk','gce_pd.go','166-207','GCE translation constructs the zonal CSI handle from pdName with unspecified project/zone, passes fsType/readOnly and uses an empty partition attribute for zero or decimal text otherwise. ReadOnly selects ReadOnlyMany rather than ReadWriteOnce.'],
 ['azureDisk','azure_disk.go','100-141','AzureDisk CSI translation supports only Managed kind. Shared, Dedicated and the default Shared pointer can pass the core API but fail migration. The URI is the CSI handle; cachingMode and fsType are attributes and readOnly is copied. diskName is not used for this handle.'],
 ['azureFile','azure_file.go','68-112','AzureFile translation builds a CSI handle using account/share/volume/namespace, passes readOnly and shareName and makes the authored Secret name a NodeStageSecretRef in the Pod namespace. Driver-specific credential keys are not validated by this translator.'],
 ['cinder','openstack_cinder.go','79-110','Cinder translation copies volumeID to the CSI handle and fsType/readOnly to CSI fields. Its inline translation does not copy the historical secretRef; that reference does not supply node credentials through this route.'],
 ['vsphereVolume','vsphere_volume.go','127-156','vSphere translation copies volumePath into the CSI handle and fsType into CSI. storagePolicyID is not used here. For nonempty storagePolicyName, this pinned implementation reads pv.Spec.VsphereVolume.StoragePolicyName after constructing only CSI, so the nil source dereference blocks this inline translation. Use a supported CSI/PVC route instead; do not claim that the policy reached the driver.'],
 ['portworxVolume','portworx.go','104-136','With CSI migration selected, Portworx translation copies volumeID/fsType into CSI and readOnly chooses ReadOnlyMany or ReadWriteOnce; the translated CSI source does not itself copy the readOnly flag. Without migration and unregister, the provider remains the registered in-tree implementation.']
];
for(const [branch,file,lines,outcome] of migrations) consumer(path=>path===`${v}.${branch}`||path.startsWith(`${v}.${branch}.`),`${outcome} The storage operator must configure the corresponding CSI driver and backend. Mounting is blocked if translation, driver registration or RPC fails; safe action is to use a driver-supported PVC/source. Follow-up is a successful replacement source translation and mount on the intended node.`,[source(`staging/src/k8s.io/csi-translation-lib/plugins/${file}`,lines,'The original inline-source translator implements this exact field conversion and selected failure branch.'),source('pkg/volume/csimigration/plugin_manager.go','56-108','Migration completion and enablement select mandatory provider migrations and conditional Portworx gates.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.nfs`),'The NFS plugin uses server:path as the mount source and adds ro only for readOnly true. It sends that source to the node NFS mounter. The node must have mount support and access to the exported server path; mount failure fails setup. The API does not supply NFS authentication credentials through a Secret child.',[source('pkg/volume/nfs/nfs.go','116-148','NFS mounter captures authored server/path/readOnly.'),source('pkg/volume/nfs/nfs.go','226-260','The actual node mount constructs server:path and ro options and handles errors.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.flexVolume`),'FlexVolume uses a dynamically discovered driver executable. It constructs standard fsType, ro/rw and volume-name options, then extra Pod/credential options, then authored options. A nonempty namespace-local Secret reference is read and data values are base64-encoded under kubernetes.io/secret/<key>. Missing client/lookup errors fail option construction. The external executable determines support for its own options and backend; failure or absent driver blocks mounting.',[source('cmd/kubelet/app/plugins.go','80-83','FlexVolume is dynamically discovered through its plugin prober.'),source('pkg/volume/flexvolume/driver-call.go','168-207','Driver options are built in standard, extra and authored order.'),source('pkg/volume/flexvolume/util.go','31-58','Secret lookup contributes base64 encoded driver secret options.'),source('pkg/volume/flexvolume/mounter.go','55-91','The mounter constructs Pod and credential options and executes the driver mount call.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.gitRepo`),'The GitRepo plugin rejects setup when GitRepoVolumeDriver is disabled. When enabled, it creates an emptyDir wrapper, executes git clone using repository and directory, and optionally checks out the supplied revision and resets hard. Git process, network or repository failure fails setup. The operator can replace this deprecated route with an init container and an emptyDir; follow-up is a successful content initialization with the intended immutable revision.',[source('pkg/volume/git_repo/git_repo.go','172-260','Original GitRepo setup checks its feature gate, emptyDir wrapper and clone/revision operations.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.lifecycle.stopSignal'),'API preparation drops stopSignal when ContainerStopSignals is disabled and no old container uses it. When enabled on the node, the runtime maps the retained named signal to a CRI enum and includes it in ContainerConfig; otherwise it sends no override. An older runtime can omit stop-signal reporting; the image/runtime default remains a separate value when no override is sent.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','856-892','Stop-signal dropping depends on the gate and old-object use.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/helpers.go','512-525','The node only constructs a signal override when its feature is enabled.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_container.go','366-391','The original container config includes a selected stop signal.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_container.go','705-714','Runtime-default reporting distinguishes older runtime support.')],['Feature-field dropping and runtime support']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${p}.securityContext.sysctls`),'The kubelet normalizes sysctl names and requires an exact or prefix allowlist match. IPC names fail with hostIPC and network names fail with hostNetwork even if allowlisted. Any failure rejects node admission with forbidden sysctl. Kernel availability and the runtime applying an admitted name/value remain node dependencies.',[source('pkg/kubelet/sysctl/allowlist.go','78-125','Original sysctl admission enforces allowlist and host namespace restrictions.')],['Node allowed/unsafe sysctl']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.securityContext.fsGroup`||path===`${p}.securityContext.fsGroupChangePolicy`,'For volume plugins that use VolumeOwnership, nil fsGroup skips permission changes. Always or nil change policy recursively applies ownership/mode updates; OnRootMismatch skips recursion only when the root directory group, permission bits and setgid already satisfy the required state. ReadOnly affects required permission bits. CSI may delegate FSGroup to a supporting driver rather than using this traversal.',[source('pkg/volume/volume_linux.go','72-87','Volume ownership changes skip nil group or a satisfied root-mismatch test.'),source('pkg/volume/volume_linux.go','149-230','Group ownership, permission bits and root mismatch checks are implemented here.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','253-275','CSI driver capability can delegate FSGroup handling.')],['Exact filesystem/runtime ownership']);

consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.fc`),'The FC plugin chooses targetWWNs plus a nonnil LUN first; otherwise it uses WWIDs with spaces replaced by underscores. Missing both routes fails setup. Node device discovery uses these identifiers; the volume is bind-mounted with ro when readOnly is true. The storage operator must expose the intended FC device to the selected node; discovery or mount errors block setup. Follow-up is successful discovery and mount of the intended device.',[source('pkg/volume/fc/fc.go','510-524','FC target precedence, WWID normalization and the no-target error are implemented here.'),source('pkg/volume/fc/fc_util.go','199-224','The node searches by WWN/LUN or WWID.'),source('pkg/volume/fc/disk_manager.go','43-99','FC setup bind-mounts the global device, adds ro and handles errors.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.iscsi`),'The iSCSI plugin converts LUN to decimal, normalizes portal addresses and preserves interface/initiator settings. A nonempty initiator name selects a volume-specific interface. Only enabled discovery or session CHAP triggers Secret lookup; successful lookup copies Secret.Data strings without enforcing a Secret type. API lookup errors fail setup. The node iSCSI client and target must support the supplied connection/authentication values; absent credentials or target/client errors can block login and mounting. The storage operator owns node/target configuration; follow-up is successful authenticated login and mount.',[source('pkg/volume/iscsi/iscsi.go','564-652','Disk construction and conditional CHAP Secret lookup implement these exact branches.'),source('pkg/volume/iscsi/iscsi_util.go','73-140','The node client uses discovery/session username, password and mutual CHAP keys.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.runtimeClassName`,'At the node, nil or empty runtimeClassName selects the empty default runtime handler. A nonempty name must resolve in the RuntimeClass cache; lookup failures stop handler resolution, otherwise its Handler is returned. API admission acceptance does not establish that the runtime supports that handler.',[source('pkg/kubelet/runtimeclass/runtimeclass_manager.go','61-78','Actual node handler resolution distinguishes default, lookup failure and RuntimeClass.Handler.')]);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${p}.securityContext.supplementalGroups`),'The kubelet adds fsGroup and explicit supplemental groups to the CRI supplemental group list, then appends extra groups supplied by the volume helper. An authored supplementalGroupsPolicy is looked up in the CRI enum; an unknown value fails context construction. Image group merge or strict handling is delegated through that policy to the runtime; image and runtime contents are external inputs, not API defaults.',[source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/security_context.go','65-87','Actual CRI group accumulation and policy lookup are implemented here.')],['Exact filesystem/runtime ownership']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.securityContext.seLinuxChangePolicy`,'When SELinuxMountReadWriteOncePod and node SELinux are enabled, the volume helper translates the effective labels of all containers using a volume. Translation errors or different labels fail this route. Recursive under the SELinuxChangePolicy gate clears the mount label; a plugin without context-mount support also clears it. A shared translated label remains the process label. This source contract requires a node SELinux implementation and the selected plugin; the operator must verify successful label translation and mount on the intended node.',[source('pkg/volume/util/selinux.go','257-313','Actual mount-label computation checks gates, label agreement, Recursive and plugin support.')],['Exact filesystem/runtime ownership']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.image`),'API preparation drops ImageVolume when disabled and no old Pod uses it. With the node gate enabled, the kubelet resolves the Pod runtime handler and calls the image puller with the authored reference/pullPolicy and Pod pull Secrets. Pull errors are retained per volume and fail creation of a container that mounts that volume; success supplies an opaque CRI ImageSpec. Registry access and runtime image-volume support remain actual external dependencies: the node operator must configure a supporting runtime and verify pull and container creation for the selected reference.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','1559-1574','Image volume preparation retains or drops the source based on gate and old-object use.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_manager.go','1745-1817','Actual image-volume pull and per-container error propagation construct the runtime ImageSpec.')],['ImageVolume feature selection']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.env[].name'),'At effective v1.35, RelaxedEnvironmentVariableValidation is locked true and selects relaxed names. The authored KubeClaw environment names also pass strict validation. The retained historical gate-off helper enables the relaxed option when a new name fails strict rules, passes relaxed rules and occurs in the old spec environment-name set; a strict-valid or relaxed-invalid name does not trigger it. Deployment updates supply the old template, but new ReplicaSet and Pod create validators supply no old template/spec. If an accepted effective gate-off configuration relies on that update compatibility, creation of the new ReplicaSet can reject its relaxed-only name before any Pod exists. Existing Deployment compatibility does not transfer to a new child.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','497-518','Pod validation options inspect the feature gate and new/old environment names.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','635-655','Exact old-name compatibility predicate distinguishes strict-valid, relaxed-invalid and previously used relaxed names.'),source('pkg/registry/apps/deployment/strategy.go','125-135','Deployment update validation supplies the old template.'),source('pkg/registry/apps/replicaset/strategy.go','111-116','ReplicaSet create validation supplies no old template.'),source('pkg/registry/core/pod/strategy.go','113-117','Pod create validation supplies no old spec or metadata.')],['Relaxed environment-name validation']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${projection}.serviceAccountToken`),'Projected token requests use the created Pod identity. Empty request audiences default to API-server configured audiences. The token endpoint checks bound-object UID, can shorten expiration to its configured positive maximum and only extends the named transition lifetime when configured, Pod-bound and targeting Kubernetes audiences. Claims/issuer errors fail issuance. The kubelet reuses an unexpired cached token on refresh failure, but fails when there is no token or it has expired; refresh is requested after 80 percent of lifetime or 24 hours with jitter. The API-server operator owns issuer/audience/lifetime configuration; successful token projection is the follow-up, not a claim that API acceptance minted a token.',[source('pkg/registry/core/serviceaccount/storage/token.go','116-125','Empty audiences use configured API-server audiences.'),source('pkg/registry/core/serviceaccount/storage/token.go','212-252','Bound UID, expiration shortening/extension, issuer failure and status lifetime are implemented here.'),source('pkg/kubelet/token/token_manager.go','109-130','Actual cache refresh failure distinguishes missing, expired and usable cached tokens.'),source('pkg/kubelet/token/token_manager.go','168-195','Refresh and expiry compare the actual returned expiration and lifetime.')],['Token issuer, audience','Token issuer']);

consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.ephemeral`),'For each created, nondeleting Pod, the ephemeral-volume controller creates a PVC named Pod-name + "-" + volume-name in the Pod namespace, copies the authored claim spec and assigns that Pod as controller owner. An existing PVC must have the same namespace and controlling Pod; otherwise this route fails. PVC API creation errors, including enabled admission/quota rejection, fail controller reconciliation. A changed Deployment template creates claim specs for future Pods; it does not rewrite or resize existing claims.',[source('pkg/controller/volume/ephemeral/controller.go','237-300','Actual controller loop, existing-PVC ownership check and namespaced PVC creation copy the template spec and return API errors.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/storage/ephemeral/ephemeral.go','41-57','Generated claim name and same-namespace controlling-Pod check are implemented here.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/resourcequota/admission.go','162-172','Enabled quota admission delegates namespaced requests to its configured evaluator.')],['PVC creation and binding remain separate receivers','The embedded PVC spec']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.ephemeral.volumeClaimTemplate.spec`),'At the PVC receiver, disabled VolumeAttributesClass can drop its field, disabled AnyVolumeDataSource can drop dataSourceRef and disabled CrossNamespaceVolumeDataSource can drop a nonempty referenced namespace, unless the corresponding old field is in use. On creation without dataSourceRef, a legacy dataSource other than core PersistentVolumeClaim or snapshot.storage.k8s.io VolumeSnapshot is cleared. With AnyVolumeDataSource enabled, a sole dataSource is copied to dataSourceRef; a sole dataSourceRef is copied back only for an absent/empty namespace.',[source('pkg/registry/core/persistentvolumeclaim/strategy.go','68-78','PVC creation preparation invokes disabled-field dropping, legacy compatibility and normalization.'),source('pkg/api/persistentvolumeclaim/util.go','37-99','Exact gate and legacy-source dropping branches.'),source('pkg/api/persistentvolumeclaim/util.go','131-190','Allowed legacy reference identity and conditional reference normalization.')]);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.ephemeral.volumeClaimTemplate.spec`),'With DefaultStorageClass admission enabled, a nil storageClassName and no legacy class annotation permit default-class selection; an explicit empty pointer counts as a chosen class and prevents this admission default. Selection errors reject; no configured default leaves it unset. The binding controller can assign a default to an unbound claim later. Without a matching PV, delayed binding waits for scheduling, a nonempty class can request provisioning, and otherwise the claim stays Pending. The storage operator owns configured class/provisioner/capacity; follow-up is a Bound claim and successful node mount.',[source('pkg/apis/core/helper/helpers.go','475-486','The actual class-presence helper counts any nonnil storageClassName, including empty.'),source('plugin/pkg/admission/storage/storageclass/setdefault/admission.go','86-119','DefaultStorageClass admission skips chosen classes, selects a default or rejects lookup errors.'),source('pkg/controller/volume/persistentvolume/pv_controller.go','328-386','Actual unbound claim reconciliation selects a match, tries retroactive defaults, waits, provisions or stays Pending.'),source('pkg/controller/volume/persistentvolume/pv_controller.go','967-1008','Retroactive default-class assignment only applies to eligible unbound claims.')]);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.ephemeral.volumeClaimTemplate.spec`),'The matching helper excludes already claimed/deleting volumes and requires enough storage capacity and matching volume mode. Enabled VolumeAttributesClass requires equal class values; disabled nonempty claim VAC errors or nonempty PV VAC is skipped. It checks an authored label selector and storage class on unbound available volumes. The scheduler path also requires matching PV node affinity and access modes; a valid prebound volume has precedence, otherwise the smallest matching capacity is selected. None of these checks creates an external data-source object or proves provisioner success.',[source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/storage/volume/pv_helpers.go','186-322','Actual PV matching checks capacity, mode, VAC, ownership, availability, selector, class, node affinity and scheduler access modes.')]);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(initPrefix),'Init containers receive the common container validator and conditional init checks. A nil per-init restartPolicy is a normal init container, whose restart behavior follows the Pod policy; Always selects a restartable init container. With AllowContainerRestartPolicyRules false, only explicit Always is accepted; with it true, Never and OnFailure also use the common policy/rule validator. Always rules require AllowRestartAllContainers. Containers without Always cannot have lifecycle or liveness/readiness/startup probes. A nonempty init resizePolicy requires AllowSidecarResizePolicy. Ordered node initialization and restartable-init handling apply before regular container startup.',[validation('3810-3872','Common init validation and exact normal/restartable init restrictions are implemented here.'),validation('3317-3349','Exact init restart policy/rule option branches.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_container.go','1270-1290','Node initialization starts the first untouched init and restores Pod-spec start order.')],['Init restartPolicy default/restrictions']);
