mechanism(path=>secPrefix.some(q=>path===q||path.startsWith(q+'.')),'os-selected-security-consumer',
 'An API-valid created Pod reaches container configuration on the selected Linux or Windows kubelet build.',
 'Linux container configuration uses the Linux CRI security synthesis. Windows container configuration uses WindowsContainerConfig: the image username supplies the initial RunAsUsername; a nonnil effective windowsOptions.runAsUserName overrides it, including an empty string. Effective gmsaCredentialSpec becomes CredentialSpec; gmsaCredentialSpecName itself is not sent as the credential bytes. HostProcess is set when effective options request it. Container Windows overrides inherit from the Pod: the gMSA pair overrides together, while username and HostProcess override independently. Windows runAsUser and runAsGroup do not set Windows RunAsUsername.',
 [source('pkg/securitycontext/util.go','44-122','DetermineEffectiveSecurityContext merges the Pod context and nonnil container overrides, including the gMSA pair.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_container_windows.go','119-146','generateWindowsContainerConfig selects image or explicit Windows username, credential bytes and HostProcess.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/security_context.go','29-155','Linux determineEffectiveSecurityContext constructs Linux CRI security fields.')]);
mechanism(path=>path.endsWith('.runAsNonRoot')||path.endsWith('.runAsUser')||path.includes('.windowsOptions'),'nonroot-os-and-image-fallback',
 'Effective runAsNonRoot is true, container security overrides are resolved, and ImageStatus returns no UID and no username.',
 'getImageUser returns an explicit zero UID when neither image identity is available. On the !windows build, without an explicit runAsUser this zero UID fails verifyRunAsNonRoot. An authored nonzero effective runAsUser passes the nonroot check; zero fails. A numeric image UID must be in 1..2147483647; a nonnumeric image username cannot establish nonroot. On the Windows build, numeric runAsUser is unsupported for this check: a present runAsUserName is compared case-insensitively with ContainerAdministrator and overrides the image check; otherwise a nonempty image username equal to ContainerAdministrator fails. An absent/empty image username does not trigger that Windows name rejection. Nil/false effective runAsNonRoot skips either OS check. Image inspection errors propagate before verification; this describes no verified image or user execution.',
 [source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/helpers.go','142-161','getImageUser propagates ImageStatus errors, prefers UID then username and returns new(int64) as root fallback.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/security_context_others.go','35-70','The !windows verifyRunAsNonRoot branch checks effective authored UID or image identity.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/security_context_windows.go','44-76','The Windows verifyRunAsNonRoot branch compares explicit or image usernames with ContainerAdministrator.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kuberuntime/kuberuntime_container.go','344-359','generateContainerConfig obtains the image user and verifies nonroot before constructing runtime configuration.')]);
// C02: selector conversion is only one stage of the trust manager.
mechanism(path=>path.startsWith(trust),'trust-selector-shared-cache-key',
 'A synchronized informer manager successfully normalizes at least one bundle for signerName S and selector {}, then looks up signerName S with nil selector before expiry or invalidation.',
 'Source deduction: LabelSelectorAsSelector converts nil to Nothing and {} to Everything, but both selectors stringify to the empty string. GetTrustAnchorsBySigner caches by signerName and selector.String(), checks the cache before listing and before optional handling, and can return the cached {} result to this later nil lookup. On a cache miss, nil matches none and fails unless optional is true; {} selects all labels, followed by exact signerName filtering. A zero-result optional cache miss returns empty bytes without adding a normalization-cache entry. A serialized selector over 100*1024 bytes fails before lookup. Successful normalization is added with cacheTTL. Informer add/update/delete invalidates the affected signer cache; the lazy selected manager uses a five-minute TTL. This conditional implementation limitation was not executed. Do not use nil as an unconditional trust-isolation control. Stop reliance on that boundary; the cluster security owner must use an explicit selector with checked matches or a named bundle, track the shared-key limitation, and later verify corrected cache-key behavior before accepting nil isolation.',
 [source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','44-46','maxLabelSelectorLength is 100*1024 bytes.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','232-278','GetTrustAnchorsBySigner serializes the key and returns cached data before List and optional/zero handling.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','100-105','Nothing.String returns an empty string.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','432-438','An empty internalSelector String joins no requirements, yielding an empty string.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','143-194','Informer events invalidate entries by signerName or by unsigned bundle name.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','399-417','Lazy manager selection supplies five minutes as cacheTTL.')]);
refine(`${trust}.labelSelector`,{omitted:'With signerName, nil converts to match nothing on a cache miss: zero results fail unless optional is true. A prior successful {} lookup for the same signer can instead supply a cache hit because both serialize to the empty key. With name, nil is required.',nullValue:'Null leaves the selector pointer nil. With signerName its cache-miss lookup matches nothing; a same-signer cached {} result can be returned first. With name, nil is required.',emptyValue:'With signerName, {} selects all labels and then exact signerName; success populates the key shared with nil. With name, every nonnil selector is forbidden.'});
