 'PostStart is called after CRI StartContainer and can race with the image process; it is not a pre-entrypoint hook. A failed PostStart records FailedPostStartHook, attempts to kill the container and returns ErrPostStartHook. Hook dispatch is Exec then HTTPGet then Sleep; a TCP-only LifecycleHandler reaches invalid handler even if accepted by API compatibility. Exec passes a zero timeout to RunInContainer; hook execution does not use probe environment expansion. PreStop runs before StopContainer only when the selected grace is positive, and its elapsed time and termination-order wait subtract from the remaining stop budget. Failed PreStop records FailedPreStopHook and does not cancel stopping. An unfinished hook is no longer awaited once the grace timer expires; the caller still gives StopContainer a minimum two-second window. Deletion grace takes precedence, then reason-specific liveness/startup probe grace can override the Pod grace, then an explicit kill override wins. Runtime stop errors propagate; no successful hook, signal delivery or application cleanup is inferred. The application/node operator must inspect hook events and stop outcomes; a failed hook requires diagnosis rather than assuming another automatic call completes its external effect.',
